<figure class="resolve" data-r16-resolve aria-labelledby="r16-resolve-title">
<figcaption id="r16-resolve-title"><span>Figure 2</span> The same request finds either outcome safely</figcaption>
<label class="choice">What happened to the first attempt? <select><option value="committed">Committed · reply withheld</option><option value="aborted">Disconnected before commit</option></select></label>
<div class="scene"><div class="request"><small>Logical purchase, across every attempt</small><code>purchase-mina-103</code><span>Mina · 1 mug + 2 tea · agreed prices unchanged</span></div><div class="sides"><div><p class="panel-label">Caller</p><strong data-live data-caller>Success reply missing</strong><span data-live data-action>Retains request key and payload</span></div><div><p class="panel-label">Database</p><strong data-live data-db>Order 103 committed</strong><span data-live data-stock>Committed stock · P3: 10 · P7: 0</span></div></div><div class="ledger"><small>Request record in the purchase transaction</small><code data-live data-ledger>purchase-mina-103 → order 103</code></div><p data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite">The caller has no confirmed result. In this selected history the database has already committed the whole purchase and its request record.</p></div>
<div class="controls"><button data-play type="button">Play</button><button data-back type="button">Back</button><button data-next type="button">Next</button><button data-reset type="button">Reset</button><output data-step></output><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
<p class="caption">Conceptual histories using the fixed stock values. The animation exposes the server’s chosen history to the reader; the caller cannot infer it from the missing reply.</p>
<details><summary>Resolution as text</summary><p>If the first attempt committed, the retry’s insertion of the same request key finds the existing record. A subsequent Read Committed statement compares the payload and returns order 103 without taking stock again. If the first attempt aborted, no request record or purchase effect remains. The retry claims the same key and performs the purchase, committing the record, stock, order and lines together. An overlapping first attempt can make that key insertion wait; absence in an earlier lookup alone does not grant ownership.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll('[data-r16-resolve]')){
 const select=root.querySelector('select');
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw(step){const committed=select.value==='committed';let caller='Success reply missing',action='Retains request key and payload',db=committed?'Order 103 committed':'First attempt aborted',stock=committed?'Committed stock · P3: 10 · P7: 0':'Committed stock · P3: 12 · P7: 1',ledger=committed?'purchase-mina-103 → order 103':'No committed request record',explanation=committed?'The caller has no confirmed result. In this selected history the database has already committed the whole purchase and its request record.':'The caller has no confirmed result. In this selected history the first transaction ended before commit, leaving no purchase effects.';
 if(step===1){caller='Reconnects to write authority';action='Same key · same payload';explanation='The retry uses the original logical identity. A new connection replaces the broken transport; the request key carries the purchase identity.';}
 if(step===2){caller=committed?'Key already recorded':'Claims the request key';action=committed?'Compare stored payload':'Perform purchase inside this transaction';db=committed?'Original order remains':'Purchase work is uncommitted';ledger=committed?ledger:'New request record, uncommitted';explanation=committed?'The unique key prevents another transaction claiming this request. Matching payload means this is a replay of the recorded purchase.':'With no committed owner, the retry inserts the key. It reserves the stock and records order 103 and both lines in the same transaction.';}
 if(step>=3){caller=committed?'Reads recorded order 103':'Commits the whole purchase';action='No second stock deduction';db='Order 103 committed';stock='Committed stock · P3: 10 · P7: 0';ledger='purchase-mina-103 → order 103';explanation=committed?'The replay returns the stored outcome. It does not rerun the stock update or create another order.':'The retry commits stock, order, both lines and the request record together. A failed transaction would discard them together.';}
 if(step===4){caller='Receives order 103';action='One logical purchase resolved';explanation='Both histories now resolve to one purchase. The identity and atomic record make resolution safe; waiting longer would not have supplied this identity.';}
 for(const [k,v]of Object.entries({caller,action,db,stock,ledger,explanation}))root.querySelector('[data-'+k+']').textContent=v;
 }});select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
}
</script>
